Drop the ALAC bool typedef that GCC 15 rejects as a redeclared keyword.

WITHOUT THIS, libsndfile 1.2.2 DOES NOT COMPILE ON THIS TOOLCHAIN. Both ALAC
codec files open with

    typedef enum
    {	false = 0,
    	true = 1
    } bool ;

which was ordinary C99 practice and is a syntax error in C23, where bool, true
and false are keywords rather than names available for redefinition. This tree
builds with GCC 15.2.0, whose default is -std=gnu23, so the two files stop the
build outright:

    error: cannot use keyword 'false' as enumeration constant
    error: two or more data types in declaration specifiers

DELETING THE TYPEDEF IS THE FIX RATHER THAN A WORKAROUND. C23 provides bool,
true and false as builtins with exactly the values this enum was defining, so
the code below it compiles unchanged and means the same thing. Nothing else in
the file is touched, and no other file in libsndfile 1.2.2 has the problem --
which is what BLFS 12.4's own build of this release establishes, since the
book carries this single change and nothing more for the same compiler
generation.

WHY A PATCH AND NOT CFLAGS=-std=gnu17. _scripts/common.sh offers that route
and names it as this tree's usual answer for code that predates C23, and it
would work here. It is not used because it is the broader instrument: it moves
the ENTIRE package back a language generation to fix two files, and it fixes
them by preserving the obsolete definition rather than by removing it. The
narrow change leaves the other ~200 source files compiling as the toolchain
intends.

The two hunks are not identical -- the encoder puts its opening brace on its
own line and the decoder does not -- so this is generated from the source
rather than written twice from memory.

Upstream: the same deletion is BLFS 12.4's libsndfile page, expressed there as
a sed over both files.
--- a/src/ALAC/alac_decoder.c	2026-08-12 02:09:53
+++ b/src/ALAC/alac_decoder.c	2026-08-12 02:09:53
@@ -38,10 +38,6 @@
 #include "ALACBitUtilities.h"
 #include "EndianPortable.h"
 
-typedef enum
-{	false = 0,
-	true = 1
-} bool ;
 
 // constants/data
 const uint32_t kMaxBitDepth = 32 ;			// max allowed bit depth is 32
--- a/src/ALAC/alac_encoder.c	2026-08-12 02:09:53
+++ b/src/ALAC/alac_encoder.c	2026-08-12 02:09:53
@@ -44,11 +44,6 @@
